Z||000000||Hank is Here||10-25-2001||01:11 AM||||Anywho, <BR> seeing that GM has been making transverse FWD cars for about 20-25 years now what are memorable collector cars for the future?  I can't think of any....maybe a Beretta GTU, Achiva SCX, Impala, or something like that. What FWD cars will be around in another 30 years?  This is really hard to think about, and also sad<P><BR>Hank ||||reg||1
Z||000001||pontiacs4me||10-25-2001||01:49 AM||||I know for a fact that the pontiac grand prix GTP- buick regal GS or anything sporting the 3800 supercharged V6 will be around for a long time.  The up and coming aftermarket, along with the L67's potential for major upgrades puts these cars in the future with definite muscle car status.  I have a feeling that within 15-20 years it will have the same status that a GN-Ttype or GNX has now.  It should be exciting to see, because a friend of mine and myself are on the forefront of technology and performance for these vehicles, these cars are the muscle cars of the future.<P>------------------<BR>Soon to be: L67 powered 87 coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||10-25-2001||02:06 AM||||How about the X-11; this "citation" was the mother of the performance Fiero...and if you check it out, it really was quite advanced for the times, and a fun car too!  I've only ever seen one in person, so I know they're not everywhere (he was on the highway, but didn't want to budge from his cruising speed of 65...sunday driver <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).<P>I agree, the Beretta GTU is a good thought along with maybe the first few models of the Z24 Cavalier.  I don't think these were as cool as the Fiero, but I may be a bit biased <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
