Z||000027||Tonker||10-26-2001||02:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>    I try to forget the fact that my fiero was made by that pathetic company.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> It's gm's best and most orginal design of the 80s and they treat it like it's trash. gm sucks!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I can't believe how the guys at the dealership seem to hate the Fiero. They say, "Don't get me wrong it's a nice little car but..."  <P>But my a$$ ( pls excuse the pun ). The Fiero is the finest GM car I have ever driven. I used to be a happy GM owner until I realised that they scrapped what should have rightfully been Pontiac's flagship car and probably the best performer in the GM lineup - Corvette be damned. <P>On the bright side I was getting my oil change at the dealership and one of the sales guys mentioned to me that he'd heard rumours - unofficial that GM might bring out the Opel Speedster in North America. Not sure if that's any more reliable than the rumours I'd already heard, though.||||reg||8
Z||000028||BN Boomer||10-26-2001||04:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<P>GM hasn't put ANYTHING awe-inspiring since 1986... Woo! a newer Corvette. Forgive me for being a little sick of that car <P><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Really? Are you serious? What happened in 1986 that was so "awe-inspiring"? What about the 88 Fiero? Or how how about the 87 Buick GNX that did the 1/4 mile in the high 13s right off the showroom floor? Car to pit an "awe-inspiring" Fiero up against one of those?<P>As for you comment about the Corvette, I'm certain there would be those with similar feelings for your beloved Fiero had it remained in production for decades. I think the Corvette has evolved into a pretty d*mn fine car myself. I just wish they were a little more affordable.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<P>Lets not see this turn into a 'American Cars are the best" thread.<P><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Conversely, let's not see it turn into a "Foreign cars are the best" thread. I'm sure that somewhere there must be a forum for the GM haters/whiners who hypocritically own a GM car. <P>And I've had guys at the local Pontiac dealer actually compliment my car and talk about a former service manager who had one with a V8 swap.<P>------------------<BR>Greg, aka Boomer<BR>Red 85 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.gmemd.com/locomotives/naf/images/sd70sm.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000029||firstfiero||10-26-2001||10:13 AM||||     Your the first one to bring up foreign cars. Your the perfect gm buyer ....You really think its cool that to rebadge pos chevy's as cady's throw in some leather an add 10 grand to the price tag? Ford does the same crap! Gee I can have a ford escort or a Mercury lynx with leather and ac for 10 grand more. hmmmmmm...decisions decisions.  <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000030||BN Boomer||10-26-2001||11:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>     Your the first one to bring up foreign cars. Your the perfect gm buyer ....You really think its cool that to rebadge pos chevy's as cady's throw in some leather an add 10 grand to the price tag? Ford does the same crap! Gee I can have a ford escort or a Mercury lynx with leather and ac for 10 grand more. hmmmmmm...decisions decisions.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Come on, I first to express what you guys are really thinking.<P>And, no, I am probably not any manufacturers "perfect buyer". Just a part of me thinks it's funny as sh!t that GM, and most other automobile manufacturers, can get away with that type of rebadging and find so many stupid consumers to fall for it.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000031||Fformula88||10-26-2001||12:35 PM||||I must respond to some of the comments posted recently.  I agree GM has built some good cars, but its not a secret that they are using parts that are more inferior now than campared to older parts.  Its also no secret there cars do not hold up as well as a whole vs a lot of other automakers.  They may be the biggest company in the world, but they have lost over 20% of the market share since 1980 and it continues to drop.  Gm had over 50% of the market, now has approximately 29%.  Thats not a sign of a great automaker but a dying one.  Boring cars aren't the only reason they are dying... who here thinks the Toyota Camry is exciting?  Yet its a top seller.  Its the quality.  Its simply not as good, and maybe buying a Chevy Cavalier you'd expect more small problems.  It is a cheaper end car.  But a Cadillac?  Nobody who buys a Cadillac wants cavaier type problems.  Thats where the Cimeron comes in.  It would be like taking a a Ford Focus, rebadging it a Lincoln whatever and expecting it to be a smaller version of an LS8.  It may have costly bells and whistles, but the same econo-car mechanicals came along, and their lack of reliability along with them.<P>Fiero identical to the Saturn?  Hardly.  You see, the thing with saturn is they took the Fiero build process of bolting plastic panels to a space frame.  Then they designed things like division specific engines not shared with any other GM vehicle.  By this point you could say the only difference between a Fiero and an MR2 is ,metal vs plastic bodies, when really they are made out of completely different parts.  Saturn belongs to GM, but it was an outside project at the start (not anymore, sadly).<P>I like GM, I wish they made better and more exciting cars.  I have also owned both foreign and domestic cars.  It has just been my experience that the foreign cars I have personally owned have been more reliable than nearly every domestic myself, or an immediate family member has owned.<P>no offense intended to anybody.  Peace  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000032||Slammed Fiero||10-26-2001||01:39 PM||||Fformula88:<P>Well said<P>We have an 87 Z51 corvette , I love it . The dash is a bit quirky but it handles amazingly , great torque. In stock form it would run 14.1's all day long. For those of you who didn't know in 84 the z51 vette was turning .99 G's on old goodyear tires. After 84 they toned down the z51 package.<P>I'm not a Gm hater , we own a lot of their vehicles. My beef is that they put billions into the development of Caddies and Corvettes , while they let the cheaper cars grow old and stagnent.<P>If you took the new cavalier z24 , put a good suspension under it and brought back the 190hp quad 4 , you would have a killer car! The car looks great , just needs more to back up the looks.<P>They have the technology , they have the parts. It all gets cut off at the knees when you hit the bean counters..telling people what they want instead of asking them.<P>Look at honda , when they redesigned the new civic , they went around and measured Civic owners garages , and average weight..and all sorts of things.<P>finding a cheap car that is fun to drive like the Fiero is hard. And the Fiero has it's fare share of shortcomings , but it's still a fun car to drive.<P>Remember when a GTI was cheap? These things are a blast to drive. Now the price is 35 grand!<P>The subaru WRX , no doubt a great car for the money. But here in Canada if I want to get one off the showroom floor it's gonna cost me nearly 40 grand!.<P>Miatas in 1989 were cheap ..now ..40+ grand here in the north.<P>I haven't lost my love for GM , but my love stems from cars that are no longer in production. Gm has all the resources to build a cheap , fun car for the masses..there too busy with there heads up their asses designing stuff like the aztek.<P>Anyone who has driven an Austin Mini knows what a fun car is all about.<P>JM ||||reg||1
