Z||000038||Elvira||10-26-2001||03:51 PM||||How about the X-11; this "citation" was the mother of the performance Fiero...and if you check it out, it really was quite advanced for the times, and a fun car too! <P>They definitely were fun!  Chester and I bought an 84 X-11 in 86 and we put 200k miles on it and dragged it around with us when we moved,  even though it was trashed in the flood when we lived in Kentucky.  It took us getting Chester's 86GT to finally ditch the X-11 to the boneyard.  Other than the our Fiero, which there is NO comparison to, the X-11 was second on our list of favorite cars that we owned.<P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||1
