Z||000040||87GT||10-26-2001||08:53 PM||||Ive noticed that looking at Consumer Reports that one of the best performing American cars is the Chevy Prizm compact car.  The reason why?  It's a Toyota Corolla!!  Its sold as a Chevy but interior and exterior is almost identical to a Corolla so that is why its ratings were so much better.  I also read somewhere that the new Pontiac Vibe is going to be sporting the 1.8 liter Toyota motor found in Celica GTs.  I guess Toyota and GM have some sort of a partnership.  Are you guys ready for a Pontiac with a Toyota motor?? ||||reg||1
Z||000041||GTFiero1||10-26-2001||10:04 PM||||the only ONLY beef i have with gm is they usetoo much plastic in the interior, thats why GM cars aren't doing as good as expected, i read an article on it that Cadillac is selling over seas but dont make a lot of sales because they say that theres too much plastic compared to BMW and such. we have an 87 cadillac and im not sure if theres anything in the interior thats plastic. if it is plastic, they've wrapped it in leather and vynal. what happended to this? well, i actually have too beefs, the other one is they dont change there designs enough anymore, if you look back from the 70's down to the early 1900's, the car design changed every year and they sold great. the cadillac eldorado has been the same design since 1992...personally i think oldsmobile has the best looking cars now,but there being shut down<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000042||Fformula88||10-27-2001||12:16 PM||||The Pontiac Vibe in partnership with Toyota is another example of where GM has dropped the ball on what could really be an exciting car.<P>The Celica GT-S 180 HP motor can be had in it.  There is also going to be AWD available as an option.  Can you get the 180 HP engine and AWD together?  Nope!  You can get the heavy AWD version with the weaker 140 HP engine, combined with this cars higher weight than the Celica should equal a real dog.  The 180 horse engine with AWD could make this thing a real blast... come on GM.  Wake up!||||reg||1
Z||000043||Pontiaddict||10-28-2001||02:00 AM||||The reason you can't get a Vibe with the 180hp motor and the AWD is because GM felt that the 140hp motors torque would be better suited to the AWD car. GM will be selling dealer installed superchargers for the 140hp motor that would boost the hp to something like 180 or 190 hp. If you play your cards right with the option sheet, you might get more hp cheaper than by just getting the 180hp toyo motor from the beginning.||||reg||1
